From: Steamac maintainers <steamac@fxgam.es>
Subject: [PATCH] MSL: preserve component names with sparse raster width links

STEAMAC-87/BB regress after MoltenVK 0053 / SPIRV-Cross 0058 (8959e4b).
The ordinary raster path supplies only width mismatches in outputs_by_location
and inputs_by_location. The old component-name workaround treats a nonempty
map as a complete active interface, so an unrelated Component=2 or 3 loses its
suffix. Both members become user(locnN), which Metal rejects as a duplicated
user-defined name / invalid vertex return type. Captured 1.9.14 shaders contain
user(locn2/* HACK _2*/) and the same failure is reproduced at pipeline creation.

With the opt-in width linker, preserve the SPIR-V component suffix on both
vertex outputs and fragment inputs independently of the sparse adapter maps.
Keep exact width lookup and all legacy component-name handling unchanged.
There is no new cache metadata: MoltenVK 0053 already keys the adapter maps
exactly, and the build's patch-series hash changes pipelineCacheUUID.

sentry-87-components.sh exercises float2+float2 (plain and interface-block) and
float3+float next to equal/wider/narrower linked varyings. Shipped 1.9.14 fails
12 of 24 draws with duplicate names; equal-width controls render correctly.
Each run serializes/reloads the pipeline cache and reverses the pipeline order.

---
diff --git a/spirv_msl.cpp b/spirv_msl.cpp
--- a/spirv_msl.cpp
+++ b/spirv_msl.cpp
@@ -16918,7 +16918,9 @@ string CompilerMSL::member_location_attribute_qualifier(const SPIRType &type, uint
 			bool active_input  = type.storage == StorageClassInput  && ( inputs_by_location.empty() ||  inputs_by_location.find({locn, comp}) != end( inputs_by_location));
 			bool active_output = type.storage == StorageClassOutput && (outputs_by_location.empty() || outputs_by_location.find({locn, comp}) != end(outputs_by_location));
 
-			if (active_input || active_output)
+			// Width-link maps are sparse adapters, not complete active-interface lists.
+			// Keep the same component name on both sides even without a width adapter.
+			if (msl_options.pad_stage_interface_components || active_input || active_output)
 			{
 				quals += "_";
 				quals += convert_to_string(comp);
